==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge]]s spawn, delay 10~166.67 seconds<sup>300f~5,000f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Snache]]s (4,000%) spawn, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Snache]]s (8,000%) spawn, delay 20~30 seconds<sup>600f~900f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Manic Mohawk Cat (Enemy)|Manic Mohawk Cat]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Teacher Bear]]s spawn, delay 73.33~80 seconds<sup>2,200f~2,400f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Master A.|Master As]] spawn, delay 80~86.67 seconds<sup>2,400f~2,600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
A very useful interaction for this stage is a [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Tank Cat]] at '''level 24 or with unit defense up [[Cat Combo|combos]]''', which allows it to have enough health to survive a hit from Manic Mohawk Cat without support. That may not sound like much, but it dramatically reduces his ability to push. Naturally, your [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cat]] should also be at least level 20+10 to survive a weakened Manic Mohawk hit; 20+23 can survive two without weakening. You could in theory use Eraser to [[cheese]] the stage along with [[Li'l Tank Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Eraser]] on the initial peons, but this takes far too long and far few levels to be helpful. [[Warlock and Pierre (Uber Rare Cat)|Warlock & Pierre]] or other [[Attacks Only]] Units like [[Takeda Shingen (Uber Rare Cat)|Takeda Shingen]] and [[Mighty Rekon Korps (Uber Rare Cat)|Orbital Annihilator Ragnarok]] could be used to cheese the level as well with enough stacking.

Alternatively, you can simply choose to pin Manic Mohawk at the base using units like [[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Deadeye]] and [[Lone Cat and Kitten (Rare Cat)|Vendor Cat]], while using LD units to chip away at the base and destroy it, as the base only has a third of Manic Mohawk's health and will crumble long before itself.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Ancient Egg: N001 (Special Cat)|Haniwa Cat]]: Haniwa Cat is a great meatshield for this stage since it is spammable with Research Combos, is Resistant to Traitless and doesn't have to worry about non-targeted threats.
*[[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]]: With extremely high range and slowing capabilites, he will very easily stall Manic Mohawk and the support to a crawl. The blindspot allows him to easily be stacked at the start.
*[[Onmyoji Cat (Rare Cat)|Thaumaturge Cat]]: Guaranteed weaken from a safe range prevents Manic Mohawk from pushing further and dealing heavy damage to your frontline. Pre-TF may work, though with less effectiveness.
*[[Driller Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Driller Cat]]: Similar to Thaumaturge, but with a MUCH stronger weaken effect (Weakens enemies to 10% of their attack rather than 50%!) and can also be stacked like Cyberpunk thanks to the blindspot. Do note that the uptime isn't 100%, unlike Thaumaturge, so stacking and other attackers are still needed.
*[[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance]] and [[:Category:Wave Attack Cats|Wave Attackers]]: They are very important here, as they can hit the enemies behind Manic Mohawk Cat, preventing them from stacking.
*[[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Recruit]]: Can push back Manic Mohawk by knocking him back, and can synergize well with Cyberpunk by pushing him back into the range of Cyberpunk. His True Form is also very useful, also slowing down Manic Mohawk and granting range for extra insurance. Do note he may push your units into the range of Master A. if he is not managed properly.
*[[Freshman Cat Jobs (Super Rare Cat)|Prof. Cat Jobs]]: With his guaranteed weaken to 1% with high uptime, Cat Jobs can reduce Manic Mohawk's damage to a laughable 139. Its damage being effectively none lessens the pressure put on your meatshields, and allows units who would otherwise get juggled to death a chance to strike. However, he suffers from Single Attack and very low health, meaning he should not be relied upon as your sole source of crowd-control. Additionally, his abysmally long cooldown means you won't get a second chance.
*[[Lone Cat and Kitten (Rare Cat)|Vendor Cat and Kitten]]: Similar to Sniper the Recruit, however he also has a brief freeze effect that can stop Manic Mohawk for a second. The [[Bombergirl (Deadly)|stage]] where you get this unit is also relatively easy, so most players would likely have him by now.

===Recommended Ubers===
*[[Ninja Girl Tomoe (Uber Rare Cat)|Ninja Girl Tomoe]]: Her LD attacks and anti-Traitless specialty are quite useful, being able to hit everything from a safe distance and temporarily freeze everything on the field.
*[[Balaluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Piccolan Pasalan]]: Having its true form will make stalling Manic Mohawk as well as all the peons in this stage far easier. However, its abysmal attack frequency holds them back from being particularly potent compared to other crowd-control options.
*[[Asiluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Assassinlan Pasalan]]: Similar to Piccolan Pasalan, they can easily stall Manic Mohawk effectively acting as a secondary Cyberpunk on the stage that can't be stacked at the beginning. They also have a [[Long-Legged (Combo)|medium slow combo]] that boosts the slow from it and Cyberpunk.
*[[Radiant Aphrodite (Uber Rare Cat)|Megaphrodite]]: With her insanely potent [[Long Distance]] attacks, she's capable of effortlessly sniping the Master A.s and Teacher Bears from a relatively safe distance. This prevents major threats from stacking up to the point of becoming impossible to handle.
*Any [[EPICFEST (Gacha Event)|EPICFEST]] uber: Given the fact that they all specialize in anti-Traitless damage, Crowd Control, or both, it should be self-explanatory why they work excellently here. Additionally, all of them outrange Manic Mohawk as well.
*[[Kubiluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Kubilan]] or [[Kaoluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Kaolan Pasalan]]: These are two very useful ubers that, provided with enough support, push manic mohawk back and reduce his pushing power, potentially keeping behind the base, effectively softlocking him there and allowing your units to chip at the base.
*[[Koneko (Uber Rare Cat)|Superstar Koneko]]: You can utilize her Wave, Surge, and Explosion to pierce up to Master A and Teacher Bear, dealing high damage via Crit/Savage Blow. She also has a Slow against Traitless, letting her stall the main threats of the stage somewhat consistently with her AoE attacks. Make sure to protect her well, since her recharge rate is LONG.

